    pr_ref:  # 1d77
    description: "**Elixir protocols (`defprotocol` / `defimpl`) are unmodelled, and their functions are mis-named.** WI-fisug-vamij-sulij-zubiz-goboh-kivik-gazuv-lovat is `done` with the title \"detect @behaviour and defimpl protocol implementation edges\", but its closure note covers only `@behaviour` and the table, and `elixir.py` contains no `defimpl` / `defprotocol` handling (grep, dev @ 4dfb1d645a). Repro (elixir analyzer, 2026-10-01):\n\n    defprotocol Size do\n      def size(data)\n    end\n    defimpl Size, for: Map do\n      def size(map), do: map_size(map)\n    end\n    defmodule Outer do\n      defimpl Size, for: Outer do\n        def size(_), do: 0\n      end\n    end\n\nEmitted: `function size` TWICE with no module (the protocol's bodyless declaration and the Map impl), and `function Outer.size` (the nested impl attributed to `Outer`, whose real module is `Size.Outer`). No module symbol for `Size` or for either impl module, no type relationship, no protocol-function -> impl `dispatches_to`.\n\nCounts (grep, 2026-10-01): `defimpl` plausible 20, livebook 17, phoenix 10, nex-framework 6; `defprotocol` files plausible 1, livebook 4, phoenix 1, nex-framework 1.\n\nFix direction: `defprotocol P` -> module symbol P with its `def` heads as declaration symbols (same marking WI-vitas gives `@callback`: kind function, `modifiers=[\"abstract\"]`, out of call resolution); `defimpl P, for: T` -> module `P.T` owning its defs, `implements` P, and P.f -> P.T.f `dispatches_to`. Bare-name and mis-owner symbols are an identity defect independent of the edges."  # 1d77
    fields: {}  # 1d77
